@0    = ~Whoops - hey, watch out there, you almost walked into me! You want to lean on my shoulder a second?~
@1    = ~I'm fine, I'm fine! I'm just feeling the darkness a little, that's all.~
@2    = ~I know what you mean.~
@3    = ~You do? But you always seem okay in these places. I mean, you say you're nervous and all, but when I see you striding along like that, it's kind of inspiring.~
@4    = ~It is? I mean, yeah, of course it is.~
@5    = ~Was that a rustle? I heard something in that corner! Can I hide behind you?~
@6    = ~Don't grab me like that! You'll make me jump out of my skin!~
@7    = ~Okay, okay. I promise I won't.~
@8    = ~Right. You stay behind me, and I'll - er, I'll make sure nothing gets at you.~
@9    = ~(I've never been inspiring before. Am I doing okay?)~
@10   = ~(You're doing great!)~
@11   = ~No, no. No, you can't seriously tell me that was an ogre. Sounds like an orc at most.~
@12   = ~It's true. Seriously, true. True as the eyes on my face.~
@13   = ~...which are looking mighty close together right now.~
@14   = ~C'mon, Keto, why won't you believe me?~
@15   = ~'Cause I see you using that line on every girl, and it's not going to work on me. No matter how many drinks you buy me.~
@16   = ~Oho, no you don't. I'm not having you nosing around in my backpack.~
@17   = ~I just want to see what you've been scribbling. What have you been writing about me in that book of yours?~
@18   = ~Wouldn't you like to know!~
@19   = ~Yes! I do! Come on, pretty please?~
@20   = ~If you think puppy-eyes will work on me...you're right. Go on, then, have a peek.~
@21   = ~"Shifty-eyed"? "Canny"? That's not exactly complimentary.~
@22   = ~Canny's a compliment...well, sort of.~
@23   = ~Not exactly. What happened to "charming smile"? "Engaging grin"? Er, what else...~
@24   = ~"Toothsome dentures"? I'll add that in, then...~
@25   = ~Hey!~
